#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119567 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f5c9c30-1745-5986-b116-e9e70a7c6161" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Vector"}] :question/id #uuid "ba897e22-8104-5772-a0d3-9b062f3592f1" :question/math-academy-id "e-4932" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point $P(-3,2,1)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $\\mathbf{n}= \\langle 0, 2, 0 \\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $\\mathbf{p}=\\langle -3,2,1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{n}=\\langle 0,2,0 \\rangle$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(x_0,y_0,z_0)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $\\mathbf{n}$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(\\mathbf{r} - \\mathbf{p}) \\cdot \\mathbf{n} = 0,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{r}$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $\\mathbf p$ is the position vector of $P.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,2,0⟩ & =⟨-3,2,1⟩\\cdot ⟨0,2,0⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,2,0⟩ & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119568 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0d93156-f9be-5e6e-976a-bef30dc892ee" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector That Is Parallel To a Plane"}] :question/id #uuid "a33f6c43-4e25-5d67-9f73-ca99a18fb434" :question/math-academy-id "e-4933" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $\\langle 0,\\, \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{b}, \\: \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{c} \\rangle$ is parallel to the plane $\\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\langle 2, -1, 4 \\rangle  = 3.$ What is the value of $\\dfrac{b}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $\\mathbf{v} = \\langle t_1,t_2,t_3 \\rangle$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $\\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\langle 2, -1, 4 \\rangle  = 3$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $\\mathbf{n}=\\langle 2, -1, 4 \\rangle.$ So, $\\mathbf{v} \\perp \\mathbf{n}$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨2,-1,4⟩ & =0 \\\\ 2{t}_{1}-{t}_{2}+4{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =2{t}_{1}+4{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v}=\\langle t_1, 2t_1 + 4t_3, t_3 \\rangle,\n$$\n\nwhere $t_1,t_3 \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$ \n\nWe are told that the first component of $\\mathbf{v}$ equals $0.$ So, we must set $t_1=0.$ \n\nSince $\\mathbf{v}$ is nonzero, we can pick any $t_3 \\neq 0.$ For example, setting $t_3=1$, we get\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v} = \\langle 0,\\, \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{4}, \\, \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{1} \\rangle.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\dfrac{b}{c} = 4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119569 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45cdbb0d-2986-5c05-8d23-dce29363051b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Straight Line"}] :question/id #uuid "43586a83-879c-5caf-9063-a8f4afbb8b4c" :question/math-academy-id "e-4935" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(\\sqrt{2},0,-5)$ and is perpendicular to the line\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3 \\\\ y=-1+\\sqrt{3}t \\\\ z=5-t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vector of $Q$ is $\\mathbf{q}=\\langle \\sqrt{2},0,-5 \\rangle.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/assets/4c70e51d85874e5a241a5d9b35b147500d4c306187c5e0a1d15a48a9aef07706.png)\n\nThe direction vector of the line is $\\mathbf{v}=\\langle  0 , \\sqrt{3} , -1\\rangle,$ so a normal vector to the plane is \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{n}=\\mathbf{v}=\\langle  0 , \\sqrt{3} , -1 \\rangle.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,\\sqrt{3},-1⟩ & =⟨\\sqrt{2},0,-5⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\sqrt{3},-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,\\sqrt{3},-1⟩ & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316889 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45cdbb0d-2986-5c05-8d23-dce29363051b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Straight Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc8a9931-4b41-5c66-9d98-fcf79c4820c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,2,3⟩=22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316891} {:answer/id #uuid "347d57a2-fbb7-5583-bb16-786d4e1ae381" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,3,2⟩=14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316892} {:answer/id #uuid "013eae6a-093f-5868-8fc4-0d2b8abb0040" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨6,2,2⟩=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316893} {:answer/id #uuid "7c7607c9-f26a-5689-8932-61774fb7d075" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨3,2,2⟩=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316894} {:answer/id #uuid "88e38b3b-d0e0-5930-b8b9-dd2485c127b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,6,2⟩=12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316895}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "013eae6a-093f-5868-8fc4-0d2b8abb0040" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨6,2,2⟩=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316893} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f9ca81e-819f-5a83-8bcc-efef9d6aa0a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316890}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "78e0dc1f-5e12-54f0-b00c-492a979933d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-127937" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(2,-1,3)$ and is perpendicular to the line that goes through the points \n$A(-4,1,3)$ and $B(2,3,5).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨2,-1,3⟩.$\n\nSince the line  passes through the points $A(-4,1,3)$ and $B(2,3,5)$ we can find a vector parallel to the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨2,3,5⟩-⟨-4,1,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,2,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨6,2,2⟩.$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨6,2,2⟩ & =⟨2,-1,3⟩\\cdot ⟨6,2,2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨6,2,2⟩ & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316896 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45cdbb0d-2986-5c05-8d23-dce29363051b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Straight Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d1083a7-8ac3-5e89-9c34-77320f55a409" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-3,4,1⟩=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316898} {:answer/id #uuid "3eed3c19-8e3e-504d-8d6e-7979b366f1ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,4,3⟩=11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316899} {:answer/id #uuid "24c06ecf-5904-5987-bbad-17a96f7593f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-4,3⟩=15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316900} {:answer/id #uuid "0d17c3cb-71a1-5e7d-bc66-618007380fe9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-4,3,1⟩=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316901} {:answer/id #uuid "acef90b4-5796-578f-8f57-aaba20ba47ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨3,1,4⟩=13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316902}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d1083a7-8ac3-5e89-9c34-77320f55a409" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-3,4,1⟩=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316898} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8739ff2-6b64-5141-8eae-d81ba06fd6a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316897}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "47335439-5d39-5166-8bb4-814a188345e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-127944" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(-1,1,2)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=5-3t \\\\ y=2+4t \\\\ z=-3+t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨-1,1,2⟩.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=5-3t \\\\ y=2+4t \\\\ z=-3+t\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,⟨x,y,z⟩=⟨5,2,-3⟩+t\\text{ }{{⟨-3,4,1⟩}_{⏟}}_{v}.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe direction vector of the line is $v=⟨-3,4,1⟩,$ so a normal vector to the plane is \n\n$$\nn=v=⟨-3,4,1⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-3,4,1⟩ & =⟨-1,1,2⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,4,1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-3,4,1⟩ & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316903 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45cdbb0d-2986-5c05-8d23-dce29363051b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Straight Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b40b62f9-f45d-5d3f-a5cf-678820eea359" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-2,4⟩=22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316905} {:answer/id #uuid "7cd3a595-2dde-5063-906b-d1b04e1d20b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨4,-2,1⟩=18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316906} {:answer/id #uuid "1a3c2917-e957-5938-b145-2a4f805fb0bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,-2,1⟩=15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316907} {:answer/id #uuid "1d5d8a0f-8eff-5258-8da6-ac9b0c88e753" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-4,-2⟩=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316908} {:answer/id #uuid "68ff1c28-aac5-52bb-92b7-b6bdc4b84f44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-2,2,1⟩=12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316909}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a3c2917-e957-5938-b145-2a4f805fb0bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,-2,1⟩=15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316907} :answer-field/id #uuid "54bfcd08-ed0e-55e3-ad80-4da66ceab7db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316904}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7d127c10-f6e2-5a96-ab28-c3201569ee57" :question/math-academy-id "q-127956" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(4,-2,3)$ and is  perpendicular to the line \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1+2t \\\\ y=3-2t \\\\ z=5+t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨4,-2,3⟩.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1+2t \\\\ y=3-2t \\\\ z=5+t\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,⟨x,y,z⟩=⟨-1,3,5⟩+t\\text{ }{{⟨2,-2,1⟩}_{⏟}}_{v}.\n$$\n\n   \n\nThe direction vector of the line is $v=⟨2,-2,1⟩.$ So, a normal  vector to the plane is \n\n$$\nn=v=⟨2,-2,1⟩.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,-2,1⟩ & =⟨4,-2,3⟩\\cdot ⟨2,-2,1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,-2,1⟩ & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316910 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f5c9c30-1745-5986-b116-e9e70a7c6161" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06f1af3d-5221-526c-b154-3c9fd1bd6615" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨3,2,0⟩=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316912} {:answer/id #uuid "1a4c26dc-3ada-521c-8825-0fd68d31f270" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-2,5⟩=⟨3,2,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316913} {:answer/id #uuid "d8cc3533-f514-5e58-9f6d-5ea7ba6900cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-2,5⟩=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316914} {:answer/id #uuid "6a41782d-6b08-556f-9f95-018f0be10c74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-1,2,5⟩=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316915} {:answer/id #uuid "99c40fd1-4cf8-536c-821f-622d9cfca3f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨3,2,0⟩=⟨-1,2,-5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316916}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8cc3533-f514-5e58-9f6d-5ea7ba6900cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-2,5⟩=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316914} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4815878-051e-5124-a4df-b62f40ff5bb7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316911}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a8d650e6-dfa8-594c-8c20-f63e265d1d5b" :question/math-academy-id "q-33026" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point  $Q(3,2,0)$ and is  perpendicular to the vector $n=⟨1,-2,5⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨3,2,0⟩,$ and $n=⟨1,-2,5⟩$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes though the point $Q({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(r-q)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $q$ is the position vector of $Q.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,-2,5⟩ & =⟨3,2,0⟩\\cdot ⟨1,-2,5⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,-2,5⟩ & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316917 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f5c9c30-1745-5986-b116-e9e70a7c6161" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43c7d742-9499-5f29-91d2-b9920fb9a36c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316919} {:answer/id #uuid "d65e7cbe-fab5-5020-ae76-91046be0e73a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316920} {:answer/id #uuid "e76958a4-f0a9-564b-b572-e6bb6c971a20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316921} {:answer/id #uuid "83cfbb99-4e21-5151-9ce0-5c9a0b8bd96a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316922} {:answer/id #uuid "a7902d5d-7344-529d-a001-8ae963229f7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316923}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7902d5d-7344-529d-a001-8ae963229f7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316923} :answer-field/id #uuid "35db1012-2955-55e0-8997-945a65a2c3e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316918}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "36530b79-821b-5731-b1ff-cff3103bd6a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-33027" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point $Q(1,2,-1)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ and $n=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes though the point $Q({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(r-q)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $q$ is the position vector of $Q.$\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316924 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f5c9c30-1745-5986-b116-e9e70a7c6161" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3eaf8f8-7097-5813-aa5e-e25608cae2b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot (8i+\\sqrt{27}j)=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316926} {:answer/id #uuid "c9cc72c3-2094-5b60-8da4-0c265a053104" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot (8i+\\sqrt{27}j)=8-\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316927} {:answer/id #uuid "4c4dc8ac-265b-5859-bd26-1f14645e1b92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot (i-\\sqrt{3}j+4k)=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316928} {:answer/id #uuid "a019abae-b534-5000-925a-c53619cadbb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot (8i+\\sqrt{27}j)=i-\\sqrt{3}j+4k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316929} {:answer/id #uuid "34b081fc-d6d8-560a-aec4-1d8e18d448b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot (i-\\sqrt{3}j+4k)=8i+\\sqrt{27}j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316930}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3eaf8f8-7097-5813-aa5e-e25608cae2b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot (8i+\\sqrt{27}j)=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316926} :answer-field/id #uuid "e831398f-b760-5aca-b42c-a530021e9259" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316925}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "00fbf737-6bbe-5465-9125-1b11baeb7ec1" :question/math-academy-id "q-33035" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point  $P(1,-\\sqrt{3},4)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=8i+\\sqrt{27}j.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=i-\\sqrt{3}j+4k$ and $n=8i+\\sqrt{27}j$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes through the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as \n\n$$\n(r-p)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $p$ is the position vector of $P.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot (8i+\\sqrt{27}j) & =(i-\\sqrt{3}j+4k)\\cdot (8i+\\sqrt{27}j) \\\\ r\\cdot (8i+\\sqrt{27}j) & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316931 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f5c9c30-1745-5986-b116-e9e70a7c6161" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72a19bb8-0aca-580c-afa4-03b4ac9e35f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨3,2,2⟩=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316933} {:answer/id #uuid "ae1fe646-46cf-51c7-9b0e-f0d83b96bee6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,2,3⟩=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316934} {:answer/id #uuid "732176b2-44ae-5a70-b2eb-af7b8907e33d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨3,3,2⟩=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316935} {:answer/id #uuid "5376dab4-36c0-5cb9-9c8a-6145e85d5897" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,3,3⟩=⟨3,2,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316936} {:answer/id #uuid "17400030-8ff4-574f-b581-15a6623c0e17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,3,3⟩=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316937}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae1fe646-46cf-51c7-9b0e-f0d83b96bee6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,2,3⟩=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316934} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6216fdb-ceae-536b-bdf2-c5cf55b5a6b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316932}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a59a738a-2841-5e3f-b750-020d46e95380" :question/math-academy-id "q-33312" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point $Q(3,2,2)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=⟨2,2,3⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨3,2,2⟩,$ $n=⟨2,2,3⟩$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes though the point $Q({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(r-q)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $q$ is the position vector of $Q.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,2,3⟩ & =⟨3,2,2⟩\\cdot ⟨2,2,3⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,2,3⟩ & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316938 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f5c9c30-1745-5986-b116-e9e70a7c6161" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6bdf2793-33e5-54d3-97af-3a4169fa10bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot (6i+5j+4k)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316940} {:answer/id #uuid "a305a2b0-31a6-5914-8d1e-75a647e69670" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot (6i+5j+4k)=52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316941} {:answer/id #uuid "7dd05887-56ef-5433-8f15-02181089229c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot (6i+5j+4k)=5i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316942} {:answer/id #uuid "b9e614bd-555a-5877-8017-c9580c67ae75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot (5i+2j+3k)=52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316943} {:answer/id #uuid "6024122d-f1c6-5b4c-80f3-5d0fc03976b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot (5i+2j+3k)=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a305a2b0-31a6-5914-8d1e-75a647e69670" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot (6i+5j+4k)=52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316941} :answer-field/id #uuid "be8fe33a-fe3e-5bbf-b05f-981cf643ed07" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316939}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "de06b04b-9864-5c8f-bac6-c6b5019acb9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-33322" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point  $Q(5,2,3)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=6i+5j+4k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=5i+2j+3k$ and $n=6i+5j+4k$ is normal to the plane. \n\nThe equation of the plane that passes though the point $Q({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(r-q)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $q$ is the position vector of $Q.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot (6i+5j+4k) & =(5i+2j+3k)\\cdot (6i+5j+4k) \\\\ r\\cdot (6i+5j+4k) & =52.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316945 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0d93156-f9be-5e6e-976a-bef30dc892ee" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector That Is Parallel To a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "981dfb58-67c7-5fc1-857c-5130a1025a19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316947} {:answer/id #uuid "21c08ac4-f18c-5cca-8cce-4078edd46041" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316948} {:answer/id #uuid "07df3a7c-58ae-5914-a86a-2766b6e91cf0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316949} {:answer/id #uuid "2b36ef70-047d-5703-a20b-55f3873f45dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316950} {:answer/id #uuid "ea2399af-b73f-5d9f-8b0f-85f631dbd8dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21c08ac4-f18c-5cca-8cce-4078edd46041" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316948} :answer-field/id #uuid "4520247f-7e44-5a2e-ad85-a0b3a504acb6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316946}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "50a00e03-bb56-54e1-be3b-f6563f49a100" :question/math-academy-id "q-70814" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $⟨0,\\,b,\\,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨1,-2,1⟩=10.$ What is the value of $\\frac{b}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨1,-2,1⟩=10$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨1,-2,1⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨1,-2,1⟩ & =0 \\\\ {t}_{1}-2{t}_{2}+{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{3} & =2{t}_{2}-{t}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}{t}_{1} \\\\ {t}_{2} \\\\ 2{t}_{2}-{t}_{1}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{2}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the first component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{1}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{2}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{2}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨0,\\,1,\\,2⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{b}{c}=\\frac{1}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316952 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0d93156-f9be-5e6e-976a-bef30dc892ee" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector That Is Parallel To a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55b65f9f-ec53-5046-a8f8-5a2b9d8d7b23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316954} {:answer/id #uuid "495da882-e478-58fc-8eb5-34716a1ede65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316955} {:answer/id #uuid "34c0f37b-6301-592d-b699-1b34db6040bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316956} {:answer/id #uuid "5a7b8fc7-7935-57c1-8d9f-149e95f64ed8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316957} {:answer/id #uuid "fb3e2ce9-819c-5cc5-b515-6e8521c2b38c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316958}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55b65f9f-ec53-5046-a8f8-5a2b9d8d7b23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316954} :answer-field/id #uuid "a52a55d1-00eb-509c-b5d3-bd83b058ea7f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316953}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ffbac4ff-c800-546e-a3b3-644d72310aa4" :question/math-academy-id "q-70817" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $⟨a,\\,0,\\,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨3,0,1⟩=5.$ What is the value of $\\frac{a}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨3,0,1⟩=5$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨3,0,1⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨3,0,1⟩ & =0 \\\\ 3{t}_{1}+{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{3} & =-3{t}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},-3{t}_{1}⟩\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{2}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the second component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{2}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{1}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{1}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨1,\\,0,\\,-3⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{a}{c}=-\\frac{1}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120435 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0d93156-f9be-5e6e-976a-bef30dc892ee" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector That Is Parallel To a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4bff29e-8a55-5152-bd5e-c28937dbd187" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119086} {:answer/id #uuid "c406bae9-4652-564b-8df2-406d995a5d35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119087} {:answer/id #uuid "c5e667c5-21b7-59a1-b4ad-12b289d841d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119088} {:answer/id #uuid "168f6906-cead-5d6d-9a98-9eb3f88fa6f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119089} {:answer/id #uuid "6b0659b9-afa6-5125-833a-15bb73ab7574" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119090}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b0659b9-afa6-5125-833a-15bb73ab7574" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119090} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2c9baab-9c48-5d09-ac05-3fd6629fd144" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119085}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f1725487-2c6d-5d22-95bb-183dbe4038eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-70821" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $⟨a,\\,0,\\,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨3,-3,1⟩=-12.$ What is the value of $\\frac{a}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation of the plane, $r\\cdot ⟨3,-3,1⟩=-12,$  we get the normal vector $n=⟨3,-3,1⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-3,1⟩ & =0 \\\\ 3{t}_{1}-3{t}_{2}+{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{3} & =3{t}_{2}-3{t}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},3{t}_{2}-3{t}_{1}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{2}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the second component of $v$ eqauls $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{2}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{1}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{1}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨1,\\,0,-3⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{a}{c}=\\frac{1}{-3}=-\\frac{1}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316959 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0d93156-f9be-5e6e-976a-bef30dc892ee" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector That Is Parallel To a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bdc19efe-e83f-535d-b7bc-269f52dfe7f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316961} {:answer/id #uuid "91c4e487-79de-5c11-8410-f1db1e8ce70b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316962} {:answer/id #uuid "9e891ad3-c045-5888-a683-76d86b526014" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316963} {:answer/id #uuid "3ea1439b-7092-5e79-a405-86841792d980" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316964} {:answer/id #uuid "19e37bfe-b467-581a-a2e7-d61f01846cbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316965}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91c4e487-79de-5c11-8410-f1db1e8ce70b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316962} :answer-field/id #uuid "80fa5116-035e-5df0-85fc-9df3ebaa4d29" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316960}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b1e12b5e-f23d-52bf-b80e-0e49a813bd26" :question/math-academy-id "q-70828" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $⟨0,\\,b,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨-2,2,-4⟩=15.$ What is the value of $\\frac{b}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨-2,2,-4⟩=15$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-2,2,-4⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,2,-4⟩ & =0 \\\\ -2{t}_{1}+2{t}_{2}-4{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ 2{t}_{2} & =2{t}_{1}+4{t}_{3} \\\\ {t}_{2} & ={t}_{1}+2{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},\\,{t}_{1}+2{t}_{3},\\,{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the first component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{1}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{3}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{3}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨0,\\,2,\\,1⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{b}{c}=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316966 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0d93156-f9be-5e6e-976a-bef30dc892ee" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector That Is Parallel To a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fd3b7b9-c00f-5e23-a56d-49f5c06e2136" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316968} {:answer/id #uuid "7de622e4-1179-559d-9868-86fed7a9a2c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316969} {:answer/id #uuid "1c2cc8a9-e28e-533f-bf7f-0f459cb5cdf7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316970} {:answer/id #uuid "ff90f966-b127-5050-a0e2-f4bbf9689b53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316971} {:answer/id #uuid "f78e0115-2e16-50ae-9c52-760c00875cee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316972}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7de622e4-1179-559d-9868-86fed7a9a2c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316969} :answer-field/id #uuid "78f8e23e-90e1-5a1e-b028-398ee1e15492" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316967}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "16749763-ce77-5654-ad19-901c646ee9ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-70830" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $⟨a,\\,b,\\,0⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨-1,1,-3⟩=8.$ What is the value of $\\frac{a}{b}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨-1,1,-3⟩=8$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-1,1,-3⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,1,-3⟩ & =0 \\\\ -{t}_{1}+{t}_{2}-3{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & ={t}_{1}+3{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{1}+3{t}_{3},{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the third component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{3}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{1}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{1}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨1,\\,1,\\,0⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{a}{b}=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316973 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45cdbb0d-2986-5c05-8d23-dce29363051b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Straight Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "295f1e58-4a16-5d5a-b676-984818a41fed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316975} {:answer/id #uuid "7c31152e-66dd-5fe9-9562-96be7263d661" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,1,-1⟩=⟨1,1,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316976} {:answer/id #uuid "4ea2f177-4c47-5d19-aa6d-d0bf73033d47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩=⟨2,1,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316977} {:answer/id #uuid "e4b58dd1-3b24-551d-b476-8762f33d28b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,1,-1⟩=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316978} {:answer/id #uuid "7bd83c0d-0368-5584-91e4-39648a268e3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316979}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "295f1e58-4a16-5d5a-b676-984818a41fed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316975} :answer-field/id #uuid "475d5cee-306a-5cd5-b998-795c7327de73" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316974}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "be607052-6286-5c45-a7b0-2a7d8e65a24b" :question/math-academy-id "q-70892" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(2,1,-1)$ and is perpendicular to the line that goes through the points \n$A(2,1,0)$ and $B(3,2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨2,1,-1⟩.$\n\nSince the line  passes through the points $A(2,1,0)$ and $B(3,2,1)$ we can find a vector parallel to the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨3,2,1⟩-⟨2,1,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,1,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨1,1,1⟩.$ \n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩ & =⟨2,1,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩ & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316980 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45cdbb0d-2986-5c05-8d23-dce29363051b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Straight Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d60438d6-b5d2-5d15-a6df-28caf621fd6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,1,3⟩=⟨1,-1,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316982} {:answer/id #uuid "1a565adb-24d5-50e4-bd12-79c885a09448" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,1,3⟩=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316983} {:answer/id #uuid "8f485774-81e4-5a79-8ff4-16967d44158f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩=⟨2,1,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316984} {:answer/id #uuid "6e428b4b-90f7-5cf9-9afd-0db57fee9352" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316985} {:answer/id #uuid "9d342947-b3e8-545a-9175-0c68e2ab18bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316986}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e428b4b-90f7-5cf9-9afd-0db57fee9352" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316985} :answer-field/id #uuid "427df2f4-3901-5a58-af18-9a4b43dba7bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316981}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "836af849-3232-5f71-9fa9-a73d0d879982" :question/math-academy-id "q-70894" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(2,1,-3)$ and is  perpendicular to the line \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1+t \\\\ y=2-t \\\\ z=3+2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨2,1,-3⟩.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1+t \\\\ y=2-t \\\\ z=3+2t\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,⟨x,y,z⟩=⟨1,2,3⟩+t\\text{ }{{⟨1,-1,2⟩}_{⏟}}_{v}.\n$$\n\n   \n\nThe direction vector of the line is $v=⟨1,-1,2⟩.$ So, a normal  vector to the plane is \n\n$$\nn=v=⟨1,-1,2⟩.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩ & =⟨2,1,-3⟩\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩ & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
